# Dhan access tokens live exactly 24 hours and no long-lived credential can
# replace them: the 12-month API key only MINTS a token, and minting needs an
# interactive browser login with 2FA. GET /v2/RenewToken is the only
# automatable path, and it only extends a token that is still ACTIVE.
#
# BOTH RUNS RENEW UNCONDITIONALLY (threshold 25h > the 24h token life), and
# that is the whole point rather than an oversight. Renewing at ONE fixed
# time a day sets the new expiry to that same time tomorrow, so the next
# day's run fires exactly ON the boundary - simulated across a full week, a
# single 22:00 run had Tuesday's renewal racing Tuesday's expiry at 0.0h.
# Two unconditional runs 8.8h and 15.2h apart mean the clock is reset long
# before it ever runs down. Renewing early costs nothing.
#
# TIMED TO THE EC2 SCHEDULE AND TO MARKET HOURS. The instance runs
# 08:15-23:50 IST Mon-Fri and cron does not catch up runs missed while it is
# off, so every slot sits inside that window. 02:50 UTC = 08:20 IST is before
# MCX opens at 09:00 and NSE at 09:14; 18:02 UTC = 23:32 IST is after MCX
# closes at 23:30.
#
# THE EVENING RUN PASSES --no-restart, and that is load-bearing. A restart
# only exists so running services pick up the new token, which is pointless 18
# minutes before a shutdown that re-reads the file at boot anyway - and it is
# actively dangerous, because restarting the worker kills whatever it is doing.
# On 2026-08-20 the morning renewal restarted the worker five minutes into the
# boot-time retention prune; MySQL then spent three hours rolling back 850k
# deletions, saturating the host and leaving retention seven days behind.
#
# WEEKENDS: normally the box is off and none of these fire. On a MAINTENANCE
# weekend (see docs/operations-schedule.md) it runs 09:00-18:00, and the 12:00
# UTC = 17:30 IST entry below renews then - which carries the token into
# Monday and removes that month's manual-token step. On every other weekend
# the box is off and the entry is simply never reached, which costs nothing.
#
# Fri 23:32 -> Mon 08:15 is still 56.7h against a 24h token, so on NON-
# maintenance weekends Monday continues to need a token generated by hand at
# web.dhan.co (any time after ~08:15 Sunday). Monday's run FAILS loudly with
# MANUAL ACTION REQUIRED if that has not been done.
#
# Output goes to a log (no MTA on this host); the script exits non-zero and
# logs a FAILED line on every failure path, which is the alerting surface.
50 2 * * 1-5 root /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/dhan-token-renew.sh --threshold-hours 25 >> /opt/option-decode-native/logs/dhan-token-renew.log 2>&1
2 18 * * 1-5 root /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/dhan-token-renew.sh --threshold-hours 25 --no-restart >> /opt/option-decode-native/logs/dhan-token-renew.log 2>&1

# Mid-morning safety net, 04:20 UTC = 09:50 IST. Exists because Dhan's auth
# endpoints returned 502 to the 08:20 run on two consecutive days (2026-08-17
# and 2026-08-18) - harmlessly, since nothing was consumed, but it left the
# renewal undone until 23:35 that night.
#
# Threshold 14 rather than 25 so this is genuinely a NET and not a third daily
# renewal: it fires only when the 08:20 run did not manage to reset the clock.
# After a successful 08:20 run the token has ~24h left and this exits quietly.
20 4 * * 1-5 root /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/dhan-token-renew.sh --threshold-hours 14 >> /opt/option-decode-native/logs/dhan-token-renew.log 2>&1

# Maintenance-weekend renewal, 12:00 UTC = 17:30 IST on Sat and Sun, 30 minutes
# before option-decode-weekend-stop powers the box down at 18:00 IST.
#
# Only ever fires on a maintenance weekend, because that is the only time the
# instance is running at 17:30 on a Saturday. Renewing then leaves a full-life
# token for Monday, so a maintenance weekend removes that month's manual token.
#
# --no-restart is not optional here. The maintenance window is exactly when
# long-running database work is in flight, and a restart mid-transaction is the
# failure this whole schedule was reorganised to prevent.
0 12 * * 6,0 root /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/dhan-token-renew.sh --threshold-hours 25 --no-restart >> /opt/option-decode-native/logs/dhan-token-renew.log 2>&1
